# security-posture-platform — Cursor rules

> **Superseded:** DeepSeek's delegation lane moved from Cursor to a CLI harness
> (Claude Code pointed at DeepSeek's API — see `AGENTS.md` → "Multi-model delegation").
> If you're using Cursor for ad hoc manual edits, the rules below still apply, but it is
> no longer an assigned lane in the team workflow — don't rely on it having a "role."

Read **AGENTS.md** in the repo root for the full shared context: repo layout, guardrails,
quality gates, and the multi-model delegation model.

## Capability limits — important
- Cursor itself has **no GitNexus**. Do not attempt cross-file refactors or renames that need
  call-graph awareness here — do those in Claude Code, Codex, or the DeepSeek harness instead.
- Before any risky change (touching auth, secrets, data flow, or many callers), get a
  GitNexus impact check from one of the CLI agents first.

## Guardrails (also in AGENTS.md)
- Don't commit or push unless asked. Never add `Co-Authored-By` attribution.
- Inspect files before deleting or overwriting.
- Flag any change touching authentication, secret handling, or external data egress.
- Verify edits applied; never claim an untested script works.
